# ⚙️ Installation

## 1. Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Aviral-2004/lawbot.git
cd lawbot
```

---

## 2. Create a Virtual Environment

### Windows

```powershell
python -m venv venv
```

Activate the environment:

```powershell
venv\Scripts\activate
```

### macOS / Linux

```bash
python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate
```

---

## 3. Install Dependencies

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

---

# 🤖 Local LLM Setup with Ollama

LawBot can run locally using Ollama.

Install Ollama from:

https://ollama.com/download

Then download the required models:

```bash
ollama pull deepseek-r1:1.5b
```

```bash
ollama pull nomic-embed-text
```

Make sure Ollama is running before starting the application.

---

# ☁️ Groq API Setup

LawBot can also use a cloud-based LLM through Groq.

Create a `.env` file in the project root:

```env
GROQ_API_KEY=your_api_key_here
```

Never upload your actual API key to GitHub.

Your `.gitignore` should include:

```gitignore
.env
venv/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
```

---

# ▶️ Running the Application

Start the Streamlit application:

```bash
streamlit run frontend.py
```

The application will be available at:

```text
http://localhost:8501
```

Open the URL in your browser.

---

# 💬 Using LawBot

```text
1. Start LawBot
       ↓
2. Upload a legal PDF
       ↓
3. PDF is processed
       ↓
4. Text is split into chunks
       ↓
5. Embeddings are generated
       ↓
6. FAISS index is created
       ↓
7. Ask a legal question
       ↓
8. Relevant passages are retrieved
       ↓
9. LLM generates an answer
       ↓
10. Grounded answer is displayed
```

---

# 🛡️ Hallucination Control

LawBot uses a context-grounded prompting strategy to reduce unsupported responses.

The system instructs the LLM to:

- Use the retrieved document context.
- Avoid inventing information.
- Avoid unsupported legal claims.
- Answer only when sufficient context is available.
- Clearly state when the information cannot be found in the provided document.

When the required information is unavailable, the system can respond:

```text
I don't know based on the provided document.
```

This approach helps keep generated responses connected to the source documents.

